  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1125 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nExpect mostly clear skies and dry conditions today with \nnortheasterly winds becoming light and variable this afternoon. Mid \nlevel cloudiness will increase from west to east this evening with \nincreased chances of precipitation overnight into tomorrow. The best \nchances for measurable precipitation  remain across our southern \nzones, decreasing to near zero across our northern most zones. Rain \nchances come to an end from west to east tomorrow morning with \ndecreasing clouds in the evening. Mostly clear skies are expected \novernight tomorrow night. As for temperatures, expect lows this \nmorning to range from the low 30s across west central Kansas to low \n40s across south central Kansas. Highs tomorrow are expected to \nrange form the upper 50s along the I-70 corridor to low 60s across \nthe KS/OK border. Lows will dip into the upper 30s to low 40s \ntonight with highs tomorrow in the 50s. The remainder of the forecast \nlooks dry with surface high pressure being the main feature. Highs \nduring this period will reach into the 60s for highs with upper 30s \nto upper 40s for lows.",
